# Italian letter-to-sound.
#
# One block a letter and its arms in order, the first that matches winning.
# The last arm of a block is the bare letter: what it says when nothing else
# applies. An arm may also say what must stand to its left and right without
# swallowing it -- `after', `before', and `vowel', `consonant' or `glide' in
# either place -- and `at start' or `at end' for a run that has to begin or
# end where the piece of the word does.
#
# Italian doubles its consonants and means it: a doubled letter says its
# phone twice, and that is the shape of nearly every consonant here.
#
# Thirteen are in. l, m and n are not: each passes the word gate over 20,000
# words and moves matrix cases on its own, which is the pair of gates
# disagreeing rather than either being wrong -- see docs/authoring.md.

rules in it_phone.obj named apply_ital_%s_rules
a piece runs from 712 to 872

letter b
  bb   says b b
  b    says b

letter d
  dd   says d d
  d    says d

letter f
  ff   says f f
  f    says f

letter p
  pp   says p p
  p    says p

letter t
  tt   says t t
  t    says t

letter v
  vv   says v v
  v    says v


letter r
  rr   says R     # carro -- one trill rather than two taps
  r    says r

letter j
  j    says J

letter k
  k    says k

letter w
  w    says v

letter x
  x    says k s

letter q
  q    says k

letter a
  a    says a
